IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rp-dates`
IMPORT `rp-rules`
IMPORT `rp-seat`

-- Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas), Part VII -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (rp-seat.l4) and the
-- date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's
-- output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the person with a claim in a Tasmanian class action`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

-- February 2028 has 29 days, 2027 has 28. 1 March to 1 June 2027 is 31 + 30 + 31 = 92 days.
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2028 EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2027 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 3 2027) `to` (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS 92
#ASSERT `the day before` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the day before` (`d` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 92 `days after` (`d` 10 10 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 1 2028

§§ `ss 64, 65 -- does Part VII apply`

-- Commenced on the day s 65 commenced (9 September 2019): taken as after it (fork F1). The day before: outside s 65.
#ASSERT `Does the class action law apply` `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania` (`d` 9 9 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the class action law apply` `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania` (`d` 8 9 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the class action law apply` `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the class action law apply` `a criminal proceeding` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the class action law apply` `a proceeding in another court` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 66, 67 -- starting a class action`

`civil` MEANS `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania`

-- 7 persons is enough, 6 is not; each limb of s 66(1) fails on its own.
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 6 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 250 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 7 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 7 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 1 3 2027) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where Part VII does not apply, the answer is the s 64/65 answer.
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `a criminal proceeding` (`d` 1 3 2027) 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start a class action` `civil` (`d` 8 9 2019) 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 67(3)
#ASSERT `Can I carry on although my own claim has ended` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I carry on although my own claim has ended` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 68, 69 -- being in the group`

#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `an individual, a company or another private body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `an individual, a company or another private body` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `an individual, a company or another private body` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, acting in that capacity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, acting in that capacity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `a Minister of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` `a body corporate established by law for a public purpose (not an incorporated company or association)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can a step be taken for me under incapacity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 69 does not apply: I am not under a legal incapacity`
#ASSERT `Can a step be taken for me under incapacity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, and this step may be taken by my substitute decision-maker (s 69(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can a step be taken for me under incapacity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, but this step can only be taken by a substitute decision-maker (s 69(3))`

§§ `s 71 -- opting out`

-- Class action commenced 1 March 2027; opt-out date fixed as 30 June 2027: the last day for notice is 29 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Last day to opt out` (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 6 2027
#ASSERT `Last day to opt out` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `Last day to opt out` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027

#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 6 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 4 2027) (`d` 15 4 2027) EQUALS `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 29 6 2027) EQUALS `still open: I can opt out by written notice given before the date fixed`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`
-- An extended date fixed under s 71(3) as 1 March 2028: notice on 29 February 2028 is in time, on 1 March 2028 is not.
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) EQUALS `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) EQUALS `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`

-- s 71(4): the hearing may begin on the opt-out date itself, not the day before without leave.
#ASSERT `Can the hearing begin then` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing begin then` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 29 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing begin then` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 29 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing begin then` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

